{"name":"Bud’s Sails","hex":"#e9e3d3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bud","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ntcham."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A newly sprouted leaf or blossom that has not yet unfolded.","Something that has begun to develop."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bud"},{"term":"sails","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of sail"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sailmaker on board ship."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sails"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sail","blocks":[{"text":"A sail is a tensile structure, which is made from fabric or other membrane materials, that uses wind power to propel sailing craft, including sailing ships, sailboats, windsurfers, ice boats, and even sail-powered land vehicles. Sails may be made from a combination of woven materials—including canvas or polyester cloth, laminated membranes or bonded filaments, usually in a three- or four-sided shape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Chesapeake.jpg/330px-Chesapeake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sail"},{"title":"Bud","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a bud is an undeveloped or embryonic shoot and normally occurs in the axil of a leaf or at the tip of a stem. Once formed, a bud may remain for some time in a dormant condition, or it may form a shoot immediately. Buds may be specialized to develop flowers or short shoots or may have the potential for general shoot development. The term bud is also used in zoology, where it refers to an outgrowth from the body which can develop into a new individual."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Fagus_sylvatica_bud.jpg/330px-Fagus_sylvatica_bud.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bud"}],"images":[{"srcset":"h